# This file marks THE TEMPLATE REPO ITSELF (The-AIOS/company-template).
#
# It exists so CI can tell two situations apart, because the same workflows run in both:
#
#   1. This repo — the template. It is framework infra, GPL-2.0-or-later, and it MUST
#      ship the GPL text as its root LICENSE.
#
#   2. A company repo scaffolded FROM this template by `/aios:company --create`. That repo
#      holds a company's private business context — brand, pricing, positioning, personas,
#      offerings. Per the AIOS licence policy (LICENSE-AUDIT.md § 4, "Company-distributed
#      infra — company's discretion"), that content is NOT GPL and NOT the framework's to
#      license. Such a repo must therefore NOT carry the framework's GPL as its root LICENSE.
#
# Why a sentinel and not the repo name: a legitimate FORK of the template (to contribute
# upstream) is still the template and keeps its GPL LICENSE, but its `GITHUB_REPOSITORY`
# is not `The-AIOS/company-template`. Keying on the repo name would fail every fork.
# A file that travels with forks and is removed at scaffold time is the honest discriminator.
#
# `/aios:company --create` deletes this file and moves LICENSE -> LICENSE-TEMPLATE.
# DO NOT delete it in the template repo, and DO NOT add it to a scaffolded company repo.
